**The emerging pattern is progressively sharper claim boundaries.** The productive sequence is: identify an observation's fibers; locate a target disagreement; add a justified witness; ask whether that witness can actually be acquired; optimize a declared cost; and test dynamics separately. The newer sources also correct earlier overextensions—qualified RN hypotheses, retained context versus conditioning, static parity versus Markov closure, and query cost versus physical cost. Mixed-version repositories preserve both the original wording and its repair, so filename similarity or repetition should never decide which statement governs.

| Tempting identification | What is actually supported |
|---|---|
| Hidden Quotient and toroidal parity are the same geometry | Both instantiate observation/factorization; their domains, algebraic kernels, norms, and additional structures differ |
| Any information-losing operation is a GQG `Set` quotient | Weighted marginalization and conditioning have separately declared semantics |
| Exact cocycle means autonomous dynamics | Endpoint additivity is exact even when equal current labels have unequal next laws |
| Spatial flux closure means temporal residual closure | Different variables, boundaries, and proof obligations |
| A finite sector set implies finite Markov memory | The ideal toroidal source gives an analytical counterexample |
| Fewer queries means lower latency or energy | Only if a specified implementation and measured cost model support that implication |
| Repeated documents or matching hashes corroborate a theorem | They establish shared content/provenance, not independent proof or replication |

