| 2. A practical compact toroidal predictor can achieve a specified error | Fix kernel, clock, horizon, initialization, and candidate record R. First test equal-R next-law agreement; for autonomous R test the law of **next R**, not only next q. If exactness fails, measure full-path prediction error under a declared tolerance and coverage plan | A validated collision refutes exact descent. A useful approximate predictor needs an upper-error guarantee or bounded empirical claim; a lower-bound collision alone cannot certify quality |
